/**
 * Wave 4, family 4 (24 Sept 2026): the colon, kidney and testicular entities the public list and the corpus's own
 * subtypes arrays named without a page (docs/CANCER-PAGES.md). Colon (5): colon cancer as the anatomical counterpart of
 * the existing rectal cancer page, and the WHO 2019 digestive-system histological types mucinous adenocarcinoma, signet
 * ring cell carcinoma, medullary carcinoma and serrated adenocarcinoma. Kidney (8): the WHO 2022 renal types the rcc
 * page listed as strings: collecting duct carcinoma, SMARCB1-deficient renal medullary carcinoma, TFE3-rearranged
 * (translocation) renal cell carcinoma, fumarate hydratase-deficient (HLRCC-associated) renal cell carcinoma, succinate
 * dehydrogenase-deficient renal cell carcinoma, mucinous tubular and spindle cell carcinoma, eosinophilic solid and
 * cystic renal cell carcinoma and clear cell papillary renal cell tumour. Testis (7): Leydig cell tumour, Sertoli cell
 * tumour, spermatocytic tumour and germ cell neoplasia in situ under the testicular page, and embryonal carcinoma, yolk
 * sac tumour and choriocarcinoma under non-seminoma.
 *
 * Rule cases: "kidney cancer", "testicular cancer" and "transitional cell cancer" from the public list are the existing
 * rcc, testicular and urothelial pages; "malignant oncocytoma" is not an entity in the WHO 2022 classification
 * (oncocytoma is benign, and the eosinophilic tumours that behave otherwise have their own names), so it has no page;
 * "sarcomatoid differentiation" is a feature of any renal cell carcinoma, not a type, and stays a string; the
 * postpubertal-type teratoma has too little sourced material here and is left for a later wave. Leydig and Sertoli
 * cell tumours are sex cord-stromal, not germ cell, tumours, and sit under the testicular page because that page is the
 * corpus's organ page for the testis.
 *
 * Every figure is quoted from the paper or page named beside it. Registered in src/data/index.ts as
 * cancersWave4ColonKidneyTestis.
 */
