    tldr: "Medullary carcinoma is a very rare form of bowel cancer in which sheets of poorly formed cells are packed with immune cells; almost all cases are mismatch-repair deficient and it occurs mostly in older women on the right side. Despite its ugly appearance it does at least as well as ordinary bowel cancer, and because of its immune features it is a natural candidate for immunotherapy.",
