    tldr: "Serrated adenocarcinoma is a form of bowel cancer that grows out of sessile serrated polyps rather than ordinary adenomas, keeping their saw-tooth pattern. Most cases carry a KRAS or BRAF mutation and the BRAF-mutant ones are often mismatch-repair deficient. It is treated like other bowel cancer, with the BRAF and mismatch repair results guiding drugs when it has spread.",
